# Day 6 — Relay. 30 August. Smoke from the Harrow fire. Dot is on her third night shift.
# The crew's handhelds can't reach Basin from the drainage, but they reach the ridge.

call D6_AM
  day 6
  time 06:20-12:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Readings.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. You sound tired.
DOT  Third night on. Readings, Kestrel.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_am set gave_readings -> read
  > "Not yet." -> notyet
node read
THEO Dry bulb {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}. Fuel stick {fuel}.
DOT  Copy.
goto plan
node notyet
THEO Not yet.
DOT  Fine. Smoky. That's the reading.
node plan
DOT  The Harrow crew's working the north flank, down in the drainage. Their handhelds can't reach me from in there. They can reach your ridge.
DOT  I need you up on Cinder Ridge, Kestrel. Be my ears. Relay what they say. Basin out.
do errand Climb to Cinder Ridge and relay for the Harrow crew.

call D6_RELAY
  day 6
  time 06:30-21:00
  where area:ridge
  after D6_AM
  garble
CREW Kestrel, Harrow Crew. You on the ridge? We need... — ...Basin, over.
THEO Harrow Crew, Kestrel. I'm on the ridge. Go ahead.
CREW Tell Basin we're tied in on the... — ...north flank, and we need... — ...hundred gallons at the... — ...over.
choice
  > Relay it as heard. -> m1heard
  > "Say again, Harrow?" -> m1again
  > Guess. -> m1guess
node m1heard
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Relay from Harrow Crew: tied in on the north flank, need some hundred gallons at... somewhere.
DOT  Copy. Water. They always need water. I'll find out where.
goto m2
node m1again
THEO Say again, Harrow? All after "need." Left ear's... — say again.
CREW ...Two hundred gallons at the lower spike camp, over.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Relay: Harrow tied in on the north flank, needs two hundred gallons at the lower spike camp.
DOT  Copy, two hundred at the lower spike camp. Nice and clean.
set relay_clean
goto m2
node m1guess
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Relay: north flank, two thousand gallons.
DOT  Two thousand? They'd float away. I'll send two hundred and ask.
node m2
CREW Kestrel, Harrow. Second thing. Tell Basin the... — ...is down, we're walking... — ...out by sixteen hundred, over.
choice
  > Relay it as heard. -> m2heard
  > "Say again, Harrow?" -> m2again
node m2heard
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Relay: something's down, they're walking out by sixteen hundred.
DOT  Probably the pump. It's always the pump. Copy.
goto m3
node m2again
THEO Say again, Harrow. All after "the."
CREW The pump is down. Walking the hose out by sixteen hundred, over.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Relay: their pump's down. They're walking the hose out by sixteen hundred.
DOT  It's always the pump. Copy, Kestrel.
node m3
CREW Kestrel, Harrow. Last one. Tell Basin... — ...thanks for the coffee. And tell her to go to bed. Over.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Last relay from Harrow: thanks for the coffee. And go to bed.
DOT  ...Tell Harrow copy, and mind their own business.
THEO Harrow, Kestrel. Basin says copy. And mind your own business.
CREW Ha. Copy. Harrow Crew out.
set relay_done
do errand_done
DOT  Thank you, Kestrel. You can come down off your mountain now. Basin out.

call D6_EVE
  day 6
  time 16:30-18:30
  retry 20:30
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Readings, if you're back.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_pm set gave_readings -> read
  > "Still walking." -> walking
node read
THEO Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}.
DOT  Copy. Smoke's laying down for the night. Basin out.
end
node walking
THEO Still walking.
DOT  Copy. Mind the scree in the dark. Basin out.

call D6_NIGHT
  day 6
  time 21:00-26:00
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. You awake?
THEO Basin, Kestrel. I'm awake.
DOT  Talk to me about something that isn't fire. Anything. I've had fire in my ear for three days.
choice
  > "The worst piano I ever tuned." -> piano
  > "The stairs here have a note." -> stairs
node piano
THEO The worst piano I ever tuned was in a church hall in Port Hallam. Someone had kept a cat in it.
DOT  In it?
THEO In it. For years. It had opinions about middle C.
DOT  Mm.
THEO The vicar said it had always sounded like that. That it was the sound of the parish. I said it was the sound of a cat.
DOT  ...
THEO Basin?
goto asleep
node stairs
THEO The third stair from the top rings when you step on it. Augie thought it was F. It's not.
DOT  Mm.
THEO It's E-flat. A little flat, even. Which makes it a very bad F.
DOT  ...
THEO Basin?
node asleep
THEO ...Basin?
THEO ...Goodnight, Dot.
do hiss_hold
